"enhance_help" = "How to test whisper boost…";
"enhance_instructions" = "1. Enable boost\nChoose a physical mic in this app. Turn on “Keep microphone ready” and “Boost quiet speech”. Start at +12 dB.\n\n2. Set up your dictation app\nChoose BlackHole 2ch as its microphone. If it has no device selector, change the system input to BlackHole instead; leave boost enabled with the original mic selected here. Keep music output unchanged.\n\n3. Compare results\nRead the same sentence at the same volume using the physical mic and then BlackHole. Reduce gain if noise is too loud; increase it if speech is still too quiet. Boost also amplifies noise and does not use AI denoising. Compare actual recognition results.\n\n4. Finish\nSwitch your dictation app (and system input, if changed) back to the physical mic before turning boost off. Stopping keep-alive or quitting stops this app’s audio to BlackHole.\n\nAfter relaunch, boost is off and gain resets to +12 dB. No audio is saved or uploaded. AirPods capture may still affect music quality.";
